  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Green Reforms in a Rapidly Industrialising Country: Energy Transition and Climate Smart Development in Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is designed to support the transformation of Vietnam&#x2019;s economic development model by integrating the principles of environmental sustainability and economic growth in an economy-wide framework. It will focus on developing and implementing a core set of modelling tools, data generation, increased analytical capacity through the following three set of activities
1.	Conduct policy-relevant research and analysis: to fill-in critical knowledge gaps and produce high-quality evidence that addresses pressing socio-economic policy issues proposed by the Government of Vietnam in line with stated development objectives. 
2.	Pursue policy engagement and effective communications: to ensure the research and evidence produced under the project is both policy relevant and effectively influences target audiences in ways that promote meaningful dialogue and promote broader societal and policy uptake
3.	Implement training and capacity development activities:  to ensure that researchers and analysts at Vietnam&#x2019;s key national institutions have necessary skills and tools to conduct critical data collection and analytical tasks needed for evidence-based policymaking.</narrative>
  </description>
